Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
Content-Type: text/plain;
	charset=utf-8

Hi Sean,

Outside of the Web PKI ecosystem, which is working on its own solutions, =
there are several TLS use cases that would benefit from the combined =
security of PQC and traditional ECC/RSA signatures. Apple supports =
proceeding with standardizing and allocating composite ML-DSA code =
points to unblock implementation and deployment in pursuit of these use =
cases.

Specifically, we would like to see the recommended subset of algorithmic =
combinations from draft-ietf-lamps-pq-composite-sigs [1], which balances =
the need to service different security levels against the combinatorial =
complexity of the broader set of options.

To address the specific questions on the suggested path forward:

> 1. Should the WG work on PQ + T Hybrid Signatures for TLS?
Yes

> 2. Should the WG only work on one: -pqt-dual-certs or =
-composite-ml-dsa?
Yes, just one

> 3. Should the WG work on: -pqt-dual-certs?
No

> 4. Should the WG work on: -composite-ml-dsa?
Yes

Best,
Laura Bauman


[1] =
https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-lamps-pq-composite-sigs-19.html=
#name-profiling-down-the-number-o


> On Sep 28, 2026, at 9:52=E2=80=AFAM, Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com> =
wrote:
>=20
> At IETF 126, the chairs conducted a series of polls [1] to determine =
the way forward for PQ+T hybrid signatures after hearing from the =
-composite-mldsa [2] and -pqt-dual-certs [3] authors; you can watch the =
setup, authors presentations, and the polls at [4] from around 0:16:47 =
until 1:08:00. The polls' results showed in-room consensus to 1) work on =
PQ + T Signatures for TLS and 2) work only on -composite-mldsa. The =
chairs now need to confirm this consensus on list. We are going to do =
this by asking the four questions that follow. Please take note of the =
take note of the following:
>=20
> 1. Framing of the questions is found in this deck [5]; in case it =
is/was not clear a "Yes" on Question 1 implies WG adoption of a draft.
> 2. Again, a "Yes" for 3 or 4 implies you are in favor of adopting the =
associated draft as a working group item.
> 3. Based on the responses we got during the session we only asked the =
1st 4 questions in [5].
>=20
> Please provide your answers to the following questions by 12 October =
2026:
>=20
> 1. Should the WG work on PQ + T Hybrid Signatures for TLS?
> 2. Should the WG only work on one: -pqt-dual-certs or =
-composite-ml-dsa?
> 3. Should the WG work on: -pqt-dual-certs?
> 4. Should the WG work on: -composite-ml-dsa?
>=20
> Cheers,
> spt (for the chairs)
>=20
> [1] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/polls-126-tls-202607241600/
> [2] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-reddy-tls-composite-mldsa/
> [3] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-yusef-tls-pqt-dual-certs/
> [4] https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DQp1s1UMmhTI
> [5] =
https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/126/materials/slides-126-tls-framing-=
pq-t-signatures-for-tls-00
> _______________________________________________
> TLS mailing list -- tls@ietf.org
> To unsubscribe send an email to tls-leave@ietf.org


